      "worked": "The top row gives the common sum: $8+(-6)+4=6$.\n\nThe diagonal from top left to bottom right gives the centre: $6-8-(-4)=2$.\n\nThe other diagonal gives the bottom-left cell: $6-4-2=0$.\n\nThe first column gives the middle-left cell: $6-8-0=-2$.\n\nThe third column gives the middle-right cell: $6-4-(-4)=6$.\n\nThe bottom row gives the bottom-middle cell: $6-0-(-4)=10$.\n\nCheck the remaining row and column: $-2+2+6=6$ and $-6+2+10=6$. Both diagonals also sum to $6$.",
